# ML Coding Standards

## Data Leakage Prevention
- Always fit preprocessing (scalers, encoders, imputers) on **train only**, then transform test.
- Never use target variable statistics from the full dataset — use only train fold inside CV.
- NLP embeddings: fit any dimensionality reduction on train embeddings only.

## Feature Engineering
- New features go in `src/features/engineering.py`.
- Document the intuition in a comment above the feature group.
- Use vectorized pandas/numpy operations — no row-wise Python loops on DataFrames.

## Model Training
- Use `src/validation/cross_val.py:cross_validate_model()` — do not write ad-hoc loops.
- Save all trained fold models with `src/utils/io.py:save_artifact()`.
- Always `np.clip(predictions, 0, 100)` before saving a submission.

## Configuration
- All hyperparameters live in `configs/base_config.yaml`. Never hardcode values in scripts.
- Load config with `src/utils/config.py:load_config()`.

## Reproducibility
- Set `random_state=42` everywhere a random seed is accepted.
- Log CV scores to stdout at minimum; use MLflow for tracked experiments.

## Naming
- OOF arrays: `oof_{model_name}` (e.g. `oof_lgbm`)
- Test prediction arrays: `test_{model_name}` (e.g. `test_lgbm`)
- Submission files: `data/submissions/submission_{description}_{mse:.4f}.csv`
